---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents"
  description="About: Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents. Research paper in the OpenIE research catalog."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research paper · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This is David Charlot's proposal, the Universal Law of Agency, in three layers. Agency comes first, and its definition is required. In form it is a definition plus a gate: a prediction fixed before the act, coupling to the world through intervention, consequence borne, and a joule budget that refuses any act that would break it. Nothing is an agent until the definition is met.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The kinematic bounds follow. They say how fast agency moves per second and per joule. Intelligence is the calculus of agency. It is a hindsight characteristic, read off a completed run the way velocity is read off a recorded path. It is the derivative of agency in joules.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      Energy to run is the only true metric of computer intelligence. All other factors collapse to zero. Correctness becomes the constraint: among systems that pass the gate, joules alone order them.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
      Prediction 1 gives an optimal act time for an agent that holds a goal, with a lab protocol to test it. Estimates are never measured_j. No board power is claimed.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-laws">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion papers</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Research papers: <a href="/papers/agency/" class="text-brand-cyan">Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/gates/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metered Commit Gates</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="text-brand-cyan">Task Satiation vs. Aggregate Rebound</a>.
        Essay: <a href="/papers/spellcheck/" class="text-brand-cyan">Spell Check is Global</a>.
        Product white papers, kept apart: <a href="/products/mei/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metabolic Intelligence</a> · <a href="/products/jouleos/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Search for JouleOS</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/agency/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/agency/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/agency.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
